WEBVTT

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.130
Yo.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.460
Hey.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.090
Did you remember your club enrollment form?

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.180
Yeah.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.650
You have to join for real this time, okay?

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.710
As long as <i>somebody</i> doesn't beat up the upperclassmen out of the blue.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.550
We will now begin the entrance ceremony.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.550
Our principal cannot deliver the keynote due to illness, so the Vice—

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.330
My apologies.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:42.940
The <i>acting principal</i> will be delivering the speech instead.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.900
Welcome, new students.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.230
Some of you are from our middle school,

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.870
while others have transferred from other schools.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.820
Nevertheless, I am assuming that you are all looking forward to a fresh start.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.070
Starting today, I hope that you all embrace your new lives as high school students,

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:05.490
and excel in whatever you do, be it academics or sports.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.180
Baseball transfer students?

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.540
Yeah.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.960
They built a dorm close to the school just to accommodate them,

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:52.050
and they even brought in a coach who won the Koshien a few years ago.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.280
Did you know about this, Aoba?

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.590
I heard the rumors.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.320
They must be serious about getting into Koshien.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.230
Did the old coach get fired, then?

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.400
No, but it seems like they've managed to isolate him.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.130
Isolate him?

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:10.200
They made all the non-transfer students go to tryouts,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.070
and divided the baseball team into two squads.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:15.490
Only five members from the old team, including new students,

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.180
made the first-string team.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.010
And only one was a first-year.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.170
Only one?

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:21.950
Who was it?

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:25.700
Polish these balls for us, Maki.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.100
What did you say?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.890
Do you have a problem?

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:32.570
Polishing balls and doing laundry are tasks for the Prefab squad.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.130
Seniority doesn't matter.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:39.910
And don't you ever step onto the practice field without my permission.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:41.070
You got that?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.310
Does that mean that the guy who played catcher for us didn't make it either?

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:45.840
The old captain, I mean.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:46.910
Nope.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:51.270
I don't think Akaishi ever planned on trying out.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.050
Those punks.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.700
Polish these balls, newbie.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.920
The first-stringers are ordering you to do it.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.380
Are you sure they weren't ordering <i>you guys</i> to do it?

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.360
What?

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:10.990
You got a problem?

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.800
I'm a newbie too, you know.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.890
Why don't I do it, then.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.310
Who are you supposed to be?

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.240
I'm Okubo, a first-year.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.720
I'm the manager for the Prefab squad.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.750
Please, go on with your practice.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.880
You idiot!

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.320
We can't even play stickball in a small space like this.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:39.460
They're apparently going to give you another chance before the Summer Koshien Tournament.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.430
Whoever stands out in the scrimmage game against the first-stringers

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.690
will join the team of elites.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.400
The Koshien is closer than you think.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.660
Just shut it already, you old fart.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.990
The tryouts were a bunch of crap.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:58.750
There's no way in hell that the five guys who got chosen are any better than us.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.310
That's right.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:04.930
It wasn't your skills, but your personalities that held you back, I think.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.160
What did you say, punk?

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.750
I wouldn't do that if I were you.

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:12.630
When he gets serious, he's stronger than me.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:19.160
To hell with this shitty team.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.080
I don't think so.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.770
Like I said, you have the skill.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:27.470
And we need that skill in the upcoming scrimmage.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.360
Like I care!

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.840
I'll keep you here by force if I have to.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.010
O-Old man, do something!

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:36.580
This is getting interesting, so I think I'll let it play out.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.350
And that's it for today's practice.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:01.070
Seventh-graders, bring in the equipment before heading home.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.550
Thank you for your hard work!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.630
Great job, Aoba.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:09.400
You want to go take a peek now that practice is over?

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.650
At the elite members of the high school team, that is.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.530
Hey, Manager.

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.740
Patch this up for me, will ya?

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.680
What's with that attitude?

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.180
Ah, Papa.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.070
Ahpapa?

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:38.690
Principal.

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:39.920
Acting.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.350
I'm the <i>acting</i> principal.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:43.780
But for how long?

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:47.610
You know I can't answer that.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:51.720
The principal intends to return, after all.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:56.100
Not without a release from the hospital in sight, he won't.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.960
Papa.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.240
Come on now.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.300
Didn't I tell you not to call me "Papa" on school grounds?

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.680
How do you like being the manager, Risa?

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:06.500
It's kind of boring.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.940
But I'll put up with it if I can go to the Koshien.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:14.350
Babe managers apparently don't go unnoticed around here.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.570
Rest assured, Miss.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.350
I promise I will take you there within the next three years.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.610
I'm counting on you, Coach.

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:26.410
The good old days where students would simply flock to any school have passed.

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:30.270
A renowned high school that every soul in Japan would know about...

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:34.730
That's the kind of school I want to become a principal of.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:36.910
I understand.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:40.580
Don't hesitate to let me know if you need anything to make that happen.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:43.490
We'll need two more pitching machines for now.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:47.370
And I would also like to request a fully-stocked training gym for the players.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.610
All right, I'll get it done.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.720
He looks like a good pitcher.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:55.740
That's Kamikawa, our ace pitcher.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:59.020
He has a sharp fastball and an arsenal of changeups up his sleeve.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:02.630
He can hold a game to two or three runs.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:04.060
Miki, our center fielder,

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:05.850
and Kishibe, our shortstop,

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:08.500
were both top pitchers for their respective middle schools.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.000
They'll make solid second or third pitchers.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:12.940
And then...

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:17.290
Cleanup hitter and first baseman, Azuma Yuhei.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:20.280
He's the jewel of this team, without a doubt.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.950
How is he, Aoba?

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:33.060
He's pretty good as a pitcher.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:38.730
But he doesn't get me excited.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:41.930
Hey, isn't that...

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:44.750
Take this!

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.220
Didn't I tell you not to swing so hard?

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.210
There's no room here.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.770
Hey, Chubby!

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:53.750
Bring over the balls!

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.080
Sure!

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.820
This sure <i>is</i> a small area.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.980
They really <i>are</i> being isolated.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.710
I'm leaving the middle school team to you, Miss New Captain.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.270
Are you going to go to first-string tryouts?

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:16.540
Nope.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:19.530
Unfortunately, I plan on having a stomachache that day.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:23.840
I'm not going to stay a second-stringer forever, though.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.580
We have a secret weapon up our sleeve, after all.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.450
A secret weapon?

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:49.330
Our next stop will be Mifujidai.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.290
Please be careful of the closing doors.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:04.540
Woah!

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:12.190
So <i>you're</i> the one who hit me with the bag!

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:16.780
That's not a very nice way to talk to someone who just kindly woke you up.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.330
A "thank you" would have been nice.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:20.920
You idiot!

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:24.990
How can you be in ninth grade and still not know the meaning of "kindly"?

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.080
Look!

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:27.270
I'm getting a nose bleed now.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.030
It's not like it's going to kill you.

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:31.210
Missing the stop wouldn't have killed me, either!

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:33.770
Could you keep a little bit of distance?

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.300
I don't want my friends to see us and get the wrong idea.

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:47.460
Why did you join the baseball team?

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.460
Did you say something?

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:54.210
I said, why did you join the baseball team?

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:57.170
Because I want to play baseball, of course.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.080
Oh?

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:02.610
It always seemed to me like you were just being forced to play.

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:04.420
You're right.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.950
At first, Nakanishi did drag me into playing with him.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:09.920
But this one time,

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:13.510
we played against this one pitcher who had amazing talent.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:18.920
That pitcher's form was really cool.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.860
I can't say much about her personality, though.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:28.830
She doesn't even know what "kindly" means, you know!

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:35.240
I thought to myself that it'd be so awesome if I could pitch like that, too.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.670
At least I did back then.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:39.110
If only I'd known, right?

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:52.060
If you don't like our batting center,

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:56.790
there's another one about an hour away from the station by bus,

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:57.950
Senpai.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.390
Get out of bed already, Ko!

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:18.140
You have school, remember?

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.560
<i>Why the heck did both of them die at the same time?</i>

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.870
You're not going to make it unless you start running, man.

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:45.740
Our school's pretty strict on tardies, you know.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:53.950
Close play.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:55.020
Safe by a nose!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:01.120
And today we'll be talking about—

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:03.690
<i>Fool.</i>

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:05.260
<i>You're definitely out.</i>

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.200
You there, what's your name?

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:11.640
Azuma Yuhei, #2 on the attendance list.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.100
Azuma?

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:21.410
Well then, let's get on to today's subject.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:20.930
Whoa, man.

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:27.420
This style of vernacular writing can be employed where—

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:36.490
Anyway, this style of vernacular writing can be employed...

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.040
So Ko joined the baseball team, huh?

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.970
That's what Aoba said.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:51.330
That's exciting news.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:56.530
I mean, he <i>was</i> the record holder at our batting center for quite some time.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:00.500
But things aren't going so easy for him, apparently.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:03.190
He got put into some weird squad or something.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.120
A weird squad?

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.950
What was it called again?

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.460
It was like "the dropout squad" or something...

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:11.520
Hey, Prefabber.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:12.930
Who are you talking to?

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.100
You, of course.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:19.840
The coach wants you guys to prep the field for the first string during lunch.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.140
Every day from now on.

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:25.080
You guys are the ones using it. You prep it.

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:28.080
I wouldn't disobey orders if I were you.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.540
Otherwise, they might even tear down that Prefab "farm" of yours.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:36.100
Our coach is really strict on guys with no talent, you know.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.690
Right, Azuma?

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:41.090
Who are you?

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:45.370
I'm Senda! We're in the first-string squad together!

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:47.000
I don't remember your face.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.960
You got it, Prefabber?

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:54.120
I've done my part in delivering the coach's message.

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:57.340
You should at least try to remember his face.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.780
So you're on the baseball team, huh?

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:03.420
I'm sure you don't remember me since I'm not first-string.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.070
You were running along the road this morning.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:08.760
So you do remember.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.490
What an honor.

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:14.430
And I remember seeing you back at the batting center last year.

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:20.810
You should go prep the practice field when you're done eating.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:22.930
Prefabber.

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:31.770
Don't slack off now.

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.240
The vice principal is watching.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:40.150
Apparently, he gets upset if you don't call him the acting principal.

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:43.680
I haven't heard too many good rumors about that guy.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:47.860
Rumors in this school tend to be pretty accurate.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.140
Time's up.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:01.820
Switch me in.

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:03.960
Come on, man, just a little more.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.140
I'm finally starting to get into it.

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:09.050
Don't make me waste my time.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:17.270
Hey! Smooth out the dirt in the batter's box before you go.

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:18.760
But you're left-handed!

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:20.960
So what?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.370
Azuma.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:35.070
Kubo's a potential cleanup hitter.

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.710
Don't be so harsh.

00:16:37.290 --> 00:16:38.400
Kubo?

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:41.080
The guy who was batting ahead of you.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.720
Which one is he again?

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:43.850
Come on, now.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.290
I hope you don't have your hopes set on that guy.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:53.220
I haven't been able to remember faces of people who aren't good for anything ever since I was little.

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:57.860
How many faces do you actually remember from this team?

00:16:57.860 --> 00:17:00.000
Three, no...

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:04.370
four, I think.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.280
That's not enough.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:10.570
I'll need you to remember at least eight by the time summer comes around.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:23.650
She's so cute.

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:25.490
Damn, she's cute!

00:17:25.490 --> 00:17:29.160
She's the acting principal's daughter <i>and</i> she used to live abroad.

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:33.340
Hard to believe she's the same species as <i>our</i> manager.

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:34.330
No kidding.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:36.770
Oh, our eyes met.

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:39.230
I'm liking that look.

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:43.670
It's just like the face my mom makes when she sees a cockroach.

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:45.640
Who you callin' a cockroach?

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.440
How do you like it?

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.920
I bet you've never seen an arm like that before.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:56.050
But...

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.320
I bet he'd give Akaishi a run for his money.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:17:59.120
Yeah.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.750
Akaishi?

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:01.600
Yes.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:03.790
He's a first-year catcher for the Prefab squad.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.530
The Prefab squad?

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:09.540
I don't remember seeing anyone like that at tryouts...

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.980
He didn't go.

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:16.500
There are two more tenth-graders who didn't try out, right?

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:20.300
Yeah, they all had stomachaches or something.

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:29.850
Where is everyone?

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:35.710
Oh hello, Senpai.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:38.400
Hey Chubby, where'd everyone go?

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.450
They're at the middle school training field.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.430
The middle school field?

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.370
Yes.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:47.410
Apparently, the seventh and eighth-graders can't make practice today because of some school event.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:51.290
So the middle school captain asked if we wanted to use the field together

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:53.340
so that it doesn't go to waste.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:57.850
I missed playing in a roomy place like this.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.620
She's still got it.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:04.990
She's adjusting her pitch so that each batter can find his sweet spot.

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:07.810
Watch closely, Ko.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:12.400
The way Tsukishima moves her wrists and elbows is ideal.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:15.830
Yeah, I know.

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:16.770
Move over!

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:20.230
What's this, a <i>girl</i> is pitching?

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:23.210
No wonder these crummy batters are hitting the ball so easily.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:26.510
You better put a little spirit into it when you're pitching to us!

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:29.910
Or we might just slug it all the way out into space.

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:35.550
Ooh! That pitcher's actually pretty cute if you look closely.

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:36.750
Wait, that's...

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:46.500
That's the face my mom usually makes when she's killing a cockroach.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:48.240
Let's go, Ko.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:49.640
Let's get you warmed up.

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:50.900
Throw lightly.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:51.940
Okay.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.690
That sounds a bit different.

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:09.790
It sounds a bit different from when you two were practicing secretly behind the school.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:15.730
I don't know if it's because of my age, but I don't dream that much these days.

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.430
Just one pitch will do.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:20.380
No one will notice.

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:25.240
The others haven't been on a real field for so long that they're too focused on themselves.

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:31.510
Ko!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:43.590
Azuma!

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:50.600
He saw us!

00:20:56.580 --> 00:21:00.100
Who the heck put the chalk liner here?

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.310
Nice one, Nakanishi.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:13.980
<i>We have a secret weapon, after all.</i>

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:27.190
Looks like I'll be having a good dream tonight.

00:23:06.180 --> 00:23:09.810
<i>Why are you pitching in the first-stringers' practice session, Aoba?</i>

00:23:09.810 --> 00:23:12.720
<i>She's the perfect disposable pitcher for batting practice.</i>

00:23:12.720 --> 00:23:13.650
<i>Disposable?</i>

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:15.060
<i>How can you call someone "disposable"?</i>

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:17.500
<i>Could I get a different catcher, please?</i>

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:18.280
<i>Aoba!</i>

00:23:19.030 --> 00:23:22.880
<i>So the talent that can't play in official games is going to show her mettle, huh?</i>

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:24.920
<i>Don't listen to what he's saying.</i>

00:23:25.390 --> 00:23:28.250
<i>Next time, on Cross Game Episode Seven:</i>

00:23:28.250 --> 00:23:30.320
<i>I'm a Sucker for Looks.</i>

00:23:30.320 --> 00:23:32.960
<i>I want to pitch for her and hit him as hard as I can.</i>
